## Assess, Adapt, Motivate
Teaching isn’t just the pedagogical knowledge of how to teach content, it’s understanding who you’re teaching and building on what they already know (AITSL 1.1; 1.2; 1.3). A key component of student centered, responsive teaching is differentiating the content to meet students individual needs (Maker 1982 as cited by Ashman, 2019). Using formative and summative assessment data as a temperature check for student knowledge is key to identifying the optimally accessible entry point for a unit of content (Nichols, 2021; AITSL 5.1; 5.4).
